    "detailed_description": "Isometric Chess is a challenging chess variant that expands the game into the third dimension in a unique way.<br><br>Play on a board made up of 64 <strong>cubes</strong>, each with three visible sides that represent a square in one of three dimensions.<br><br>Using orthographic projection, you can switch out of the isometric view to see a flattened version of each dimension to make better sense of how the pieces move. A piece's legal moves are first determined by their current dimension in isolation, based on the standard rules of chess. Then, any <i>empty</i> squares that share a cube with one of the current dimension's legal moves are added to the list.<br><br>Kings can not switch dimensions while in check, and you win by checkmating the king.",
    "about_the_game": "Isometric Chess is a challenging chess variant that expands the game into the third dimension in a unique way.<br><br>Play on a board made up of 64 <strong>cubes</strong>, each with three visible sides that represent a square in one of three dimensions.<br><br>Using orthographic projection, you can switch out of the isometric view to see a flattened version of each dimension to make better sense of how the pieces move. A piece's legal moves are first determined by their current dimension in isolation, based on the standard rules of chess. Then, any <i>empty</i> squares that share a cube with one of the current dimension's legal moves are added to the list.<br><br>Kings can not switch dimensions while in check, and you win by checkmating the king.",
